# Data Source: identitynow_connector

Use this data source to look up a connector by script name. It works for built-in and custom connectors.

## Example Usage

{{ tffile .ExampleFile }}

## Arguments Reference

* `script_name` - (Required) Script name of the connector.

## Attributes Reference

* `id` - Connector ID, the same as `script_name`.
* `name` - Connector name.
* `type` - Connector type.
* `class_name` - Connector class name.
* `direct_connect` - Whether sources of the connector are direct connect sources.
* `status` - Connector status.
* `connector_metadata_json` - UI metadata of the connector as a JSON object.
* `application_xml` - Application XML of the connector.
* `correlation_config_xml` - Correlation config XML of the connector.
* `source_config_xml` - Source config XML of the connector.
* `file_upload` - Whether sources of the connector are file upload sources.
